WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:15.054
needs to go for a walk," says Mother.

2
00:00:15.074 --> 00:00:18.215
"Take him for a walk around the neighborhood.

3
00:00:18.816 --> 00:00:21.217
Here's a basket and a shopping list.

4
00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:24.098
Please get everything on the list for dinner."

5
00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:29.300
So now, Happy and I are walking down the street.

6
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.602
Happy is wagging his tail.

7
00:00:32.142 --> 00:00:35.084
He loves going for a walk around the neighborhood.

8
00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:37.606
All the store owners know us.

9
00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:42.150
And Happy loves all the strange and wonderful smells.

10
00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:46.393
First, I go into the bakery.

11
00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:52.398
Mrs. Thompson always gives me a cookie with lots of chocolate chips.

12
00:00:53.139 --> 00:00:54.740
I buy some garlic bread.

13
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.281
"Bye, Mrs.

14
00:00:56.341 --> 00:00:58.063
Thompson. Thank you!"

15
00:00:58.683 --> 00:00:59.264
I say.

16
00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:01.753
There's Mr.

17
00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.073
James, the butcher.

18
00:01:03.774 --> 00:01:06.315
He's always singing Italian songs.

19
00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:08.336
He wears a white apron.

20
00:01:09.077 --> 00:01:14.099
He sells all kinds of meat: pork, beef, and chicken.

21
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.781
He throws Happy a bone.

22
00:01:17.401 --> 00:01:19.422
Happy loves the butcher shop!

23
00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:24.205
My favorite store is Purdy's Chocolate House.

24
00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:27.547
The girl who works there goes to my school.

25
00:01:28.347 --> 00:01:29.908
She is in grade seven.

26
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.941
Her mom makes the best fudge.

27
00:01:33.861 --> 00:01:37.183
Sometimes she lets me lick the spoon.

28
00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:45.266
We have two more things to get for Mommy: fish and cucumbers.

29
00:01:45.986 --> 00:01:49.448
Happy and I go to the fish market down by the river.

30
00:01:50.168 --> 00:01:54.930
The men at the fish market call out to the customers, "Salmon!

31
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.251
Two big ones!"

32
00:01:56.271 --> 00:01:58.972
"Hi, Jimmy, how's Happy?"

33
00:01:59.492 --> 00:02:00.553
the man asks.

34
00:02:02.754 --> 00:02:06.615
At the vegetable market, the cucumbers are in a basket.

35
00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:11.317
Mrs. Sanderson wipes off two cucumbers with a towel.

36
00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.539
Then she puts them in a brown paper bag.

37
00:02:15.079 --> 00:02:16.960
She also gives me an orange.

38
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.981
"Here you go, Jimmy!"

39
00:02:19.741 --> 00:02:20.501
she says.

40
00:02:22.422 --> 00:02:26.604
When we get home, Mommy is very pleased with our shopping.

41
00:02:27.424 --> 00:02:29.767
"Did the people in our neighborhood help you?"

42
00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:31.148
she asks.

43
00:02:32.049 --> 00:02:34.291
"Yes, they did," I say.

44
00:02:34.311 --> 00:02:37.254
"I got a cookie and an orange.

45
00:02:37.674 --> 00:02:39.236
And Happy got a bone!"
